RF.put("questb:b30",{"8510":{"id":8510,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Arthas' Tears!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Arthas' Tears to Sergeant Major Germaine at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Arthas' Tears Arthas' Tears in Razorfen Downs , Arthas' Tears , Spirit of Trey Lightforge 33.3 % , Treant Spirit 3.9 % and 4 more","desc":"Ok, so it looks like I still need more Arthas' Tears. I would imagine that you will be able to find them in the general location that you gathered them up for me last time. The quicker we get these, the faster we can start up the offensive against the forces at Ahn'Qiraj.\nYou gonna help us out again ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.6,"n":"Sergeant Major Germaine","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8590":{"id":8590,"t":"The Horde Needs Thick Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 54.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Leather to Sergeant Umala at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n10 Thick Leather Razzashi Cobra 37.5 % in Zul'Gurub , Felsteel Chest 7.1 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 4.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 4.5 % and 4 more","desc":"I'm glad that you decided to speak to me about this, ‹class›. It looks like the Horde's preparations for the upcoming Ahn'Qiraj War are in full swing. But you and I still need to do our part.\nI've been asked to collect a great number of thick leather skins for use in all manner of war materiel, and I need you to help me by going out there and gathering them up. There's honor and the gratitude of the Horde in it for you should you decide to help. Will you?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"‹class›, have you returned so soon with the ten thick leather that we discussed?","done":"Good work, ‹class›. I'm sure that these thick leather skins will be put to use reinforcing zeppelins and making all manner of armor and weaponry. You have my thanks, and that of the Horde. Come back again if you come across more thick leather in your travels, and luck be with you.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.1,"y":72.8,"n":"Sergeant Umala","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"510":{"id":510,"t":"Foreboding Plans","lv":34,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Foreboding Plans to Magistrate Maleb in Southshore.\nForeboding Plans\nProvided: Foreboding Plans","desc":"Among these documents is a list of requested supplies. These include mundane items (food, weapons, clothing) as well as more exotic gear (masks, oil, poison).\nBut what is most notable is the urgency of the request - these supplies were needed soon in order to undertake what is described in the document as an \"important mission against Southshore.\"","rew":"Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, you look anxious. Is there something you wish to tell me?","done":"<Maleb reads the documents.>\nThese are very troubling, ‹name›. From the information in these documents, and from the Syndicate's actions in the past, we must assume that band of cutthroats has waged war on Southshore.\nAlterac Mountains Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":58.3,"y":67.9,"n":"Syndicate Documents","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":47.9,"y":82.2,"n":"Syndicate Documents","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":48.1,"y":59.1,"n":"Magistrate Henry Maleb","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"670":{"id":670,"t":"Sunken Treasure","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Seahorn's Letter to Shakes O'Breen in Arathi Highlands.\nSeahorn's Sealed Letter\nProvided: Seahorn's Sealed Letter","desc":"Say, ‹name›, you seem to be an adventurous type. My fleet is stuck in Booty Bay until we can restock.\nThere are some heavy things brewing here and abroad and I need to get some top secret correspondence to Shakes O'Breen who is tied up off the Arathi coast.\nCan I trust you to deliver this message safely and in confidence?","rew":"Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"So was Seahorn impressed? I bet you his smile reached from Booty Bay to Ratchet.","done":"Thank you for making such a long and perilous journey. You have the gratitude of the Blackwater Raiders.\nStranglethorn Vale Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.2,"y":77,"n":"Fleet Master Seahorn","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":32.3,"y":81.4,"n":"Shakes O'Breen","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"990":{"id":990,"t":"Trek to Ashenvale","lv":19,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Raene Wolfrunner in Ashenvale.","desc":"‹name›, my mistress, Raene Wolfrunner, awaits you in the city of Astranaar within Ashenvale. With your help, perhaps we can at least ease some of the corruption that's taken hold there.\nHead south from here and stay close to the road--you'll find your way there without issue if you follow those directions.","rew":"Experience: 370\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ah, a ‹class› from Darkshore. Selarin has done well to send you here so quickly, ‹name›. I wish your trip here wasn't under such dire stress. Perhaps with your help we can improve matters.\nI would start my visit by speaking to the other citizens of Astranaar. Some could surely use your aid.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":36.6,"y":49.6,"n":"Raene Wolfrunner","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1070":{"id":1070,"t":"On Guard in Stonetalon","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Kaela Shadowspear overlooking the valley entering Windshear Crag in the Stonetalon Mountains.","desc":"Hello, ‹name›.\nYou seem to be full of wanderlust by the looks of you. Have you been to the Stonetalon Mountains? It is a land plagued by the Venture Co. and other enemies of the night elves.\nRecently, Sentinel Wolfrunner sent my friend Kaela Shadowspear there to investigate what's happening to the land, but I have yet to hear word back from her. I'm even more concerned because the Alliance sent a gnome mage along with her... a sign of trouble for sure.\nWould you find her and report back to me?","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ah, you've come from Ashenvale at the behest of Thenysil -- how I miss her, my homeland and friends. She must be doing well with the Sentinels to be sequestering adventurers for other tasks. I'm proud of her.\nIt is a pleasure to meet you, ‹name›.\nAshenvale Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.9,"y":49.8,"n":"Sentinel Thenysil","s":1},{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.9,"y":66.8,"n":"Kaela Shadowspear","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"97950":{"id":97950,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Trianna in Darnassus to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":63.6,"y":21.4,"n":"Trianna","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94350":{"id":94350,"t":"Craftsmans writ runic leather bracers","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Runic Leather Bracers\nRunic Leather Bracers","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Runic Leather Bracers, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Runic Leather Bracers Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94350","cats":["crafting"]},"94270":{"id":94270,"t":"Craftsmans writ steel weapon chain","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Steel Weapon Chain\nSteel Weapon Chain","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Steel Weapon Chain, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+125 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+125 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Sometimes friend is foe, and try to steal Ugbert's club.","done":"This weapon chain? This keep club in hand?\nUgbert thank you. Ugbert strongest ogre in all of Dustwallow!","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":40.9,"y":28,"n":"Ugbert","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"98910":{"id":98910,"t":"Darkspears basic care package","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Darkspear Raiders","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkspear Basic Care Package\nExperience: 300\n+10 reputation with The Defilers\nLevel 39 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 35 37 42 49 Side Both factions Quest ID 98910","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"4510":{"id":4510,"t":"Calm Before the Storm","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Bank Voucher to Idriana in the bank of Darnassus.\nBank Voucher\nProvided: Bank Voucher","desc":"‹name›, your help has been immeasurable. The time will come, no doubt, when I'll ask for your assistance against the silithid once more. We must absorb what we have learned in Un'Goro; I fear that my assumptions that the silithid originated from Un'Goro are now wrong... that indeed there is a far stronger presence somewhere.\nTake this note to Idriana at the bank. She'll give you something from my vault that should be viewed as a token of my gratitude. Thank you for your assistance, brave ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nOblivion Orb Snarkshaw Spaulders Eschewal Greaves\nExperience: 8,150\n+200 reputation with Alliance","back":"Elune'adore, ‹class›. What may I do for you today?","done":"This bank voucher authorizes me to withdraw an item from Gracina Spiritmight's account with us and present it to you. Congratulations would seem to be in order!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":41.8,"y":85.6,"n":"Gracina Spiritmight","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.4,"y":42.4,"n":"Idriana","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"8990":{"id":8990,"t":"The Right Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth the spirit of Isalien and slay her. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the recombined Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLord Valthalak's Amulet\nBrazier of Beckoning\nIsalien slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"It became known to us in later days, as we were doing what we could ourselves to survive, that Isalien, a night elf priestess of our company, had gone to the night elvic ancestral city, now known as Dire Maul. From what we gathered, she went there both for personal reasons and also to unlock the secrets of the piece of the amulet that she had in her possession.\nShe didn't quite make it, though. Word got back to us that she was ambushed at the Shrine of Eldretharr by Alzzin the Wildshaper and his forces.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Surely you haven't already dealt with the salvation of Isalien's spirit and the retrieval of the right piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet, ‹name›? Be sure to recombine the pieces of the amulet before handing it to me.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›, for putting Isalien's spirit to rest. Now, perhaps, she will find peace with her goddess. And, we have the reassembled amulet, as well! But we still have the hardest test ahead of us.\nIn order for the brazier to be attuned to calling forth Lord Valthalak, there are a few more items that need to be gathered and brought back to me here.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"30":{"id":30,"t":"Trial of the Sea Lion","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance. Speak with the residents of Moonglade to learn clues as to where these items may be located.\nForm the Pendant of the Sea Lion from the two pendant halves. You need to be in proximity of the Shrine of Remulos to do this.\nBring the joined pendant to Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven, Moonglade.\nPendant of the Sea Lion","desc":"For the second trial, you'll need the two halves that make the Pendant of the Sea Lion. One half draws power from the agility of the sea lion aspect, gliding through water; the other draws power from the incredible endurance of the sea lion aspect. Druids draw on both these traits equally to embody the aspect of their aquatic form.\nSpeak with the locals of Moonglade to learn where the parts may lie, and bring both here to join them together. Once formed, take the pendant to Dendrite Starblaze.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+75 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Have you formed your pendant for me to inspect, ‹name›? If you need help in locating the parts, try asking the local populace for information. Not only will you find what you seek, but it will give you a reason to explore this wondrous and sacred glade.","done":"You've completed the Trial of the Sea Lion, ‹name› - congratulations.\nEach task in acquiring the pendant shows that both agility and endurance are necessary to act in harmony with what you desire to do underwater. Neither can exist without the other, and both cannot be done without your willingness to embrace the aspect of the sea lion.\nRemember these lessons well, and count on them once you have gained your aquatic form.\nMoonglade Silverpine Forest Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":36.5,"y":40.1,"n":"Tajarri","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.6,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"830":{"id":830,"t":"The Admiral's Orders","lv":7,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Admiral Proudmoore's Orders to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill.\nAdmiral Proudmoore's Orders\nProvided: Admiral Proudmoore's Orders","desc":"You open the aged and weathered envelope and discover an official looking document. You recognize the seal of Admiral Proudmoore.\nThis looks important. Perhaps Gar'Thok, the commander of Razor Hill, would be interested in having this information.","rew":"Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"There is a look of concern on your face, ‹class›. What have you there?","done":"This does not bode well at all. You were wise to bring this information to my attention.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":59.3,"y":57.6,"n":"Aged Envelope","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":51.9,"y":43.5,"n":"Gar'Thok","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"270":{"id":270,"t":"The Doomed Fleet","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Menethil Harbor in the Wetlands, and speak with Glorin Steelbrow.","desc":"Years ago, the Third Fleet of Kul'Tiras sunk along the coasts of The Wetlands, an expanse of marsh north of the Dwarven kingdom of Ironforge. Aboard one ship was a load of Lightforge Iron.\nThis metal is precious to us, for items crafted from it strike with holy truth. If you are to face Morbent Fel, then you will need such a weapon.\nGo to Menethil Harbor and speak with my dwarven colleague Glorin Steelbrow. If that lost metal can be found, he'll know where to look.","rew":"Experience: 1,200\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Lightforge Iron is a precious metal, but it sounds like your quest is a dire one. You've come a long way, Brother/Sister. With luck, you might just find what you seek!\nAnd if you do get the iron, I know who can fashion it into a weapon against this Necromancer you speak of in Duskwood.\nStormwind City Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.9,"y":46,"n":"Bishop Farthing","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"3630":{"id":3630,"t":"Gnome Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Gnome Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Engineering at the expert level breaks into two disciplines: gnome and goblin. Gnome engineering represents by far the superior of the two! It's about the construction of wonderful gadgets and devices that make life better!\n‹name›, read this manual. If you want to learn more on gnome engineering, then take that manual to Tinkmaster Overspark in Ironforge. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure you are sure before finishing his task!","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Yes, yes, what needs of yours might I address today? Clearly, I have the time to do such since all I do is stand here while our beloved city lies in a cloud of irradiated death.","done":"Ah, a young engineer interested in pursuing the one, true discipline of engineering! Well forgive my melodrama, friend. While our situation remains dire, it still is always a good day to see another engineer respond to the clarion call of true engineering!\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.1,"y":30.3,"n":"Lilliam Sparkspindle","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.2,"y":29.2,"n":"Tinkmaster Overspark","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4110":{"id":4110,"t":"Salve via Gathering","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Fel Creep Sungrass 15 % , Mountain Silversage 15 % , Dreamfoil 15 % , Golden Sansam 15 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve","back":"A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood's corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.\nWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.","done":"Excellent work ‹name› - every bit of this, once we purify it, will help us take back Felwood. Here, take some doses of Cenarion plant salve and head into the forest. The reclaiming of the land from the corruption waits for no ‹race›!","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"9310":{"id":9310,"t":"Faint Necrotic Crystal","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 60.","obj":"Bring the Faint Necrotic Crystal to Lieutenant Rukag in the courtyard of the Undercity.\nFaint Necrotic Crystal\nProvided: Faint Necrotic Crystal","desc":"On the corpse of the fallen wight, you find a crystal that is faintly radiating necrotic energy.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBlessed Wizard Oil Consecrated Sharpening Stone","back":"Can I help you with something?","done":"You say this was taken from a wight attacking the city?\nWe have received word about the necropolis base camps that are being summoned by the Scourge. I suspect they were trying to create one in the Undercity. We will have to be vigilant in the future.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.8,"y":69.7,"n":"Lieutenant Rukag","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"3790":{"id":3790,"t":"Assisting Arch Druid Staghelm","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.","desc":"Excuse me ‹class›, but I'd like just a moment of your time if possible.\nThe Cenarion Circle in Darnassus is looking for seasoned adventurers such as yourself to lend them aid in a vital research project. While I do not know the specifics, I can inform you that none other than Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm is spearheading this research.\nPlease - if you are interested, speak with him directly in the Cenarion Enclave within Darnassus proper.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Well now, ‹class›... since you were informed that I was leading this research myself, you obviously came as quickly as you could.\nNow that you are here, be sure to pay attention the first time I tell you the details; I have no desire to repeat myself.\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54,"y":29.3,"n":"Innkeeper Firebrew","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8910":{"id":8910,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Winterspring Blood Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Shadowcraft Bracers to Deliana in Ironforge.\n15 Winterspring Blood Sample Rabid Shardtooth 30 % , Elder Shardtooth 30 % , Shardtooth Bear 30 % , Shardtooth Mauler 30 % and 4 more\nShadowcraft Bracers Scholomance Occultist 6.3 % in Scholomance , Instructor Malicia 5 % in Scholomance , Dark Shade 3.8 % , Risen Construct 3.5 % in Scholomance and 2 more","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've something that might interest you.\nI have in my possession a set of armor much like the one worn by those of your profession, but of much higher quality. I'd be willing to trade the bracers for ordinary ones in exchange for a small favor.\nThe blood of the frostsabers and bears that inhabit Winterspring has properties I'm in need of at the moment. Bring me a sizeable sample of it along with the bracers and a small amount of gold. You shall find the effort worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmantle Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you brought me what I requested of you, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent! Let's perform the trade then. It's hard to part with this excellent armor, but I'm afraid I won't be needing it any time soon.\nIf you're interested in performing more work for me, I might be willing to give up the rest of the pieces.\nDun Morogh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8670":{"id":8670,"t":"Runetotem the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":53.2,"y":43.7,"n":"Elder Runetotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1950":{"id":1950,"t":"Get the Scoop","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the phrase to Tirth's strongbox, then return to Tirth.","desc":"I can help you with the book, but first you have to help me!\nThe tome you seek is in my magically locked strongbox. To open it a special phrase must be uttered, and I can't remember the phrase! Normally my assistant helps me remember these things but he's nowhere to be found.\nIf you want my book, then find my apprentice! Ask around the race track--if you're lucky then someone has seen him. Either drag him back here, or at least get my magic phrase from him so we can open my box!","rew":"Experience: 1,850","back":"What are you waiting for? I need my magic phrase!","done":"Ah, now I remember...\nI had forgotten about that little curse I put on Johnson. I can't remember why I did it but I'm sure it served him right, the little ingrate!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.3,"y":75.7,"n":"Magus Tirth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"7070":{"id":7070,"t":"Shadowshard Fragments","lv":42,"min":39,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 39 instead of 38.","obj":"Collect 10 Shadowshard Fragments from Maraudon and return them to Archmage Tervosh in Theramore on the coast of Dustwallow Marsh.\n10 Shadowshard Fragment Shadowshard Rumbler 80 % , Shadowshard Smasher 80 %","desc":"I've recently begun testing various crystals and their arcane properties. Lady Proudmoore has given me leave to ask travelers heading into Desolace to seek out a place called Maraudon. Within the ruined temple are great elementals composed of purplish stones I've named shadowshards.\nIf you decide to head that direction and find some of the crystals, I would be very thankful. I could even fashion you a trinket from them if you so desired.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nZealous Shadowshard Pendant Prodigious Shadowshard Pendant\nExperience: 3,450\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you made the trip yet? I realize it'd be quite dangerous, but if you were successful, it would very much be worth it.","done":"These are perfect, ‹name›. I actually had other adventurers return from there also and from them I was able to fashion these... please, feel free to take one for your hard work. And thank you again for more samples to study.\nDustwallow Marsh Desolace","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Archmage Tervosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["maraudon"]},"750":{"id":750,"t":"The Hunt Continues","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grull Hawkwind in Camp Narache wants you to bring him 10 Mountain Cougar Pelts.\n10 Mountain Cougar Pelt Mountain Cougar 80 %","desc":"A tauren skilled in the ways of the hunt knows that his prey is not for mere trophy. The beasts of the plains provide us with a means of survival. You will make quite an impression on the elders if you can bring back some highly valued Mountain Cougar Pelts. You can find the beasts lurking in the hills to the south.\nOur children need clothing and our tents need mending.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nNomadic Bracers Painted Chain Belt\nExperience: 250\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"If you can provide pelts for the tribe I will pass word along to my father, Chief Hawkwind, of your generous deeds.","done":"The Tauren of Narache thank you for these provisions, ‹name›. With your skill in the ways of the hunt you will surely be revered in Thunder Bluff someday.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"98430":{"id":98430,"t":"The longwalkers","lv":8,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Help Perith Stormhoof escape Palemane Rock, and report his safety to Cairne Bloodhoof in Thunder Bluff.\nEscort Perith Stormhoof out of Palemane Rock","desc":"Hail, ‹class›. What brings you deep into such a dark and violent place?\nI was sent here by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof as a part of our efforts to communicate with the gnolls that have taken residence. The rest of my mission must remain a secret, as do all things with the Longwalkers, the trusted scouts of our chieftain.\nAll you must know is our diplomacy was met with violence, and I fear I may be tonight's feast for the gnolls if you do not help me escape.\nAre you up to the task?","done":"I am relieved that Longwalker Stormhoof is well. He is my most trusted scout, and his mission of the utmost importance.\nPlease, accept my thanks and my hospitality for riskng your life to save his own. You have done a greater service to our people than you know.\nI encourage you to explore our great city while you are here. It is a place of safety, and you will find many that may aid you on your own travels upon its bluffs.\nIsh-ne-alo por-ah.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33,"y":65.8,"n":"Perith Stormhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":59.8,"y":51.6,"n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9070":{"id":9070,"t":"Earthshatter Headpiece","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make an Earthshatter Headpiece if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Headpiece, 15 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 4 Arcanite Bars and 2 Nexus Crystals.\nDesecrated Headpiece\n15 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n4 Arcanite Bar\n2 Nexus Crystal","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Headpiece\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Earthshatter Headpiece.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9230":{"id":9230,"t":"Ramaladni's Icy Grasp","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants you to bring him 1 Frozen Rune, 1 Blue Sapphire and 1 Arcanite Bar.\nFrozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\nBlue Sapphire Alzzin's Minion 2.5 % , Rich Thorium Vein 0.8 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 0.8 % , Small Thorium Vein 0.7 % and 4 more\nArcanite Bar","desc":"Fixing this band may prove to be quite challenging, ‹name›. You see, it was made from the very runes that form inside Scourge structures - like Naxxramas. Additional materials are also required but your main concern should be getting those frozen runes. Bring me what I need and I will restore the ring to its former glory.","rew":"You will receive:\nRamaladni's Icy Grasp\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Frozen runes could probably be found inside Naxxramas.","done":"Ramaladni himself couldn't have done better! Here is the ring, as promised.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"1790":{"id":1790,"t":"The Symbol of Life","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSymbol of Life","done":"Make haste, ‹name›, more than one life hangs in the balance if you fail.\nIf for some reason you fail to help Gazin and Henze, then return to me and I will give you another Symbol of Life for your travels.\nDon't mistake my aid as simple charity, you must prove yourself worthy like any other ‹class› and continual failure may reflect upon you later.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5630":{"id":5630,"t":"Returning Home","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"Hello there, laddy/lassy. Good to see you travelin' far and wide to distant lands. No offense meant, but a lot o' your kind don't take well to these cold climates usually. Glad to see you're made of tougher stuff.\nNot too long ago one of your priestesses was in here lookin' for you--said somethin' about you finding a Priestess Alathea in the Temple of the Moon back in Darnassus. Said it was important and you should head back there soon.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards\nExperience: 210","done":"Wonderful, you've returned home, ‹name›. It always pleases Tyrande and myself when those we've trained go out into the world and return to us safely. How have things been with you? Does Elune still bless your travels? Perhaps after we speak more about the business at hand, you could tell me more of your travels.\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.3,"y":52.2,"n":"Maxan Anvol","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8830":{"id":8830,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Stormwind.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.4,"y":74.5,"n":"Officer Maloof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"78270":{"id":78270,"t":"Goblin lockpicks","lv":23,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find The Horn of Xelthos inside of Shadowfang Keep. Then, return it to C's dead drop near Pyrewood Village.\nVenture Co. Work Order","desc":"<A note sits in the chest>\nHello again, ‹name›.\nI desire a treasure known as The Horn of Xelthos, which is somewhere within Shadowfang Keep.\nVenturing inside the keep usually calls for backup. However, for this job, a low profile is of utmost importance.\nYou must go alone.\nI have a contact, by the name of Veenix, in the Stonetalon Mountains. He should be able to help you get past the courtyard gate. The rest is up to you.\nReturn the horn here, and your payment will be sent soon after.\n- C","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 210186","back":"You said you're breaking into Shadowfang...alone? You've got some guts!\nI can hook you up with explosives to get past the gate, but I'll need a work order to make it look legit on the books. An employee around here's likely carrying one. Probably someone who does a lot of tinkering or building.","done":"Nice job, ‹name›. I figure that was a cakewalk for someone in your line of work.\nAs promised, here's the goods.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":58.2,"y":51.6,"n":"Veenix","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"430":{"id":430,"t":"Return to Quinn","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 40c instead of 0.","obj":"Bring Quinn's potion to Quinn Yorick at the Ivar Patch, north of the Sepulcher.\nMinor Quinn's Potion\nProvided: Minor Quinn's Potion","desc":"Here is the potion to aid in Quinn Yorick's recovery.\nNow if you will excuse me, I have very important work to continue...","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 0 silver, 40 copper Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"My sister told me you were here to aid us. Is that true?","done":"<Quinn takes the potion and drinks it.>\nYes, I can feel it working. I will soon be able to travel.\nYou have done me a great favor, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.4,"y":12.6,"n":"Quinn Yorick","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"79950":{"id":79950,"t":"Demons and you","lv":35,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Demons and You","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 280","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nDemons and You (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"910":{"id":910,"t":"Down at the Docks","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take your ward to the docks of Ratchet in the Barrens.","desc":"I have heard tales of the mighty ships that sail between Ratchet and Booty Bay! That would be so cool to sail on the ocean and fight in many great sea battles. Maybe I will be a mighty Horde sailor when I grow up! Yeah!\nWould you take me to see the Ratchet docks, please? I promise I won't get into the water or cause any trouble - I just want to see the big boats and smell the salty sea water! Yeah!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"Are we there yet?","done":"Wow, the ocean is HUGE! There were a lot of sea gulls and stuff too - It's just as noisy and as bustling as I thought it would be. There are pirates near by too - so cool!\nThank you for taking me to Ratchet, ‹name›. That was so awesome!\nThe Barrens Open the zone on the world map Start Orcish Orphan End Orcish Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Quest ID 910\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 650 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Children's Week\nUse the Orcish Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nOrphan Matron Battlewail Orgrimmar\n2 [ 60 ] Down at the Docks this quest\nTake your ward to the docks of Ratchet in the Barrens.\nOrcish Orphan\n650 XP","cats":["special"]},"98190":{"id":98190,"t":"A friend of the family","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Menethil Statuette to Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in Stormwind Keep.\nProvided: Menethil Statuette","desc":"You'll want to take this to Stormwind right away. Proud as I am that this keep and harbor bears King Terenas Menethil II's name, we are a calm harbor in a very nasty storm of enemies. It's just not safe here.\nThe Dragonmaw in particular would sacrifice much to loot something like this... and I shudder to think of what they'd do with it.\nDon't bother going up the chain of command on this one, <lad/lass>. Go straight to Highlord Fordragon with this. He'll know where it will be best kept.\nWetlands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.8,"y":57.4,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78,"y":18,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"350":{"id":350,"t":"Look to an Old Friend","lv":31,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Elling Trias in Stormwind.","desc":"That Marzon would be contacting a member of the Defias and have ties to Lescovar...\nHaving killed VanCleef and Thredd, it would be hard to see Lescovar brought to proper justice, as your evidence is nothing without their testimonies. That is not even considering the fact that Lescovar is a noble and well connected. It effectively makes him above the law.\nYou'll need other help. I loathe to do so, but there is someone I know that will aid us. You'll find Trias in the Trade District of the city.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"You're kidding? Shaw wants my help again? Of all the nerve...\nThe Defias Brotherhood, you say? Well, you're certainly the bearer of wonderful news, aren't you? Next you're going to tell me that Deathwing is still alive and attacking the city.\nAll right, tell me everything from the beginning. And don't leave out something you think might not be important. I need to know it all.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":66,"y":74.1,"n":"Elling Trias","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"190":{"id":190,"t":"Panther Mastery","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to kill 10 Young Panthers.\nYoung Panther slain : 0/ 10","desc":"If you want to be a part of the hunt with this crack group under Hemet's leadership, you're going to need to prove yourself an able panther hunter. We'll start you out easy -- don't you worry. Let's see you kill 10 young panthers to start.\nTracking them down is only half the challenge...","rew":"Experience: 1,250","back":"A true panther hunter would be out in the fields, trying to stalk his prey. Show some commitment to your goal, ‹class›, and get back out there.","done":"Off to a good start, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.5,"n":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"110":{"id":110,"t":"Insect Part Analysis","lv":48,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Check in Gadgetzan for Alchemist Pestlezugg and his analysis of the insect parts.","desc":"I'm going to spend some time taking a look at Scrimshank's surveying gear... as well as putting his personal effects in order. I get the sneaking feeling behind my ears that this isn't the last loss we'll be facing against these bugs.\nI'd like for you to check in with Alchemist Pestlezugg to see if he has had a chance to process the insect parts we sent him. If they're ready, bring them to me.","rew":"Experience: 440\n+10 reputation with Gadgetzan","done":"Yes, I have the results right here. They are... unsettling, to say the least\nOur initial suspicion that the bugs are being controlled by an outside force, we believe, is correct. If this is the case, then we are dealing with not only a very powerful unknown force, but also a malignant one. These bugs have been changed to be pure ravagers. I've never seen anything quite like it.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2750":{"id":2750,"t":"A Bad Egg","lv":60,"min":42,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 47.","obj":"Bad Egg","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","back":"These are the eggs that cannot be saved -- they will never hatch.","done":"I am afraid I have bad news for you, ‹name›. This egg is too far gone. I can take it from you so that it may be disposed of properly.\nPlease don't be discouraged; we cannot save them all. If you find yourself in Feralas again, please try again. Bring another egg for the Super Egg-O-Matic!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":26.9,"n":"Curgle Cranklehop","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8750":{"id":8750,"t":"The Path of the Protector","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Dedication of this magnitude is a rarity. You have shown that your will is unfaltering, ‹name›. You shall be greatly rewarded for your stalwart watch over our world.\nHand me your signet ring so that I may strengthen its enchantment.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the protector!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"2990":{"id":2990,"t":"Thadius Grimshade","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Sharpbeak's Feather to Thadius Grimshade in the Blasted Lands.\nSharpbeak's Feather\nProvided: Sharpbeak's Feather","desc":"Take this feather to Thadius Grimshade, the diviner. He left Aerie Peak years ago to pursue darker knowledge, but in his heart he is still a Wildhammer!\nAnd perhaps his talents can help us find Sharpbeak.\nThis feather was taken from the nest where the gryphon child sleeps. If you give it to Thadius then, with luck, he can use his divining magics to find Sharpbeak.\nGood luck, ‹name›. You will find Thadius in the Blasted Lands, in the mage tower of Nethergarde Keep.","rew":"Experience: 2,100\n+50 reputation with Wildhammer Clan\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"‹name›, you come bearing a gift?","done":"Ah, yes. This feather belongs to a fine gryphon. One destined for great things... if he can survive into adulthood undamaged.\nYou wish to find him? Then listen close, brave ‹class›...\nThe Hinterlands Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","s":1},{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.9,"y":19.5,"n":"Thadius Grimshade","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1150":{"id":1150,"t":"Test of Endurance","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,450 experience instead of 2,400, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Grenka's Claw to Dorn Plainstalker in Thousand Needles.\nGrenka's Claw Grenka Bloodscreech","desc":"I'm pleased to see your courage remains steadfast in light of what you've already done. Since your faith is intact, the time has come to test your body.\nFirst is a test of endurance. Go to the Roguefeather Den west of Freewind Post. Make your way to the depths of their lair and destroy their foodstuffs. By then you should have provoked their fury, and if you are able to survive long enough, Grenka Bloodscreech herself will come for you--kill her and bring me her claw to complete your test.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"You must be prepared spiritually, physically and mentally for the challenges that lie ahead of you.\nToo often do we rush forward before we are ready. I consider it my duty to the youth, no matter which tribe they belong to, to prepare them for the dangers they may face after they leave the sanctity of their home.","done":"Grenka was powerful, even by troll standards. You should be proud of your accomplishment this day.\nDuring your test of faith you displayed strength of spirit, and now you have shown endurance in battle by taking on the Roguefeather harpies, but the time has come for a new test.\nThousand Needles Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":53.9,"y":41.5,"n":"Dorn Plainstalker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"590":{"id":590,"t":"A Rogue's Deal","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Calvin Montague in Deathknell.","desc":"What?\nWhat?!\nYou want money? I don't owe you any money.\nLetter? What letter? Oh, you wanna fight then? All right, mate... let's do this! Owe you any money...","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 0 silver, 25 copper Experience: 110\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"Incredible! What skill!\nThought you'd be easy prey, ‹name›. Got me good, you did.\nHere's the coin I promised... not as much as I said it'd be, but that's on a count o' me lying to ya in the first place.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":38.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Calvin Montague","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"5150":{"id":5150,"t":"Dadanga is Hungry!","lv":55,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"15 Bloodpetal Sprout Stone Guardian , Tar Creeper , Tar Lord , Tar Beast and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nSmall Brown-wrapped Package","back":"Dadanga looks up at you as you approach her. She seems to be hoping for something...\nShe's probably hungry!\nThere's got to be something growing in the crater that would be just the perfect snack for a large herbivore. Dadanga's a big girl; whatever you bring her, there would need to be a lot of it!","done":"Placing the sprouts in front of her, Dadanga seems pleased.\nShe nudges a small brown-wrapped package towards you, in exchange for the treat!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":43.6,"y":7.2,"n":"Dadanga","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1470":{"id":1470,"t":"Piercing the Veil","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Venya Marthand 3 Rattlecage Skulls.\n3 Rattlecage Skull Rattlecage Skeleton 80 %","desc":"Greetings, child. I can see that you are still young in the ways of the warlock, power still eluding your grasp. I can sense your eagerness to learn.\nAnd you will learn.\nThere is no strength in ignorance. Knowledge is our greatest power. Through its application, we can control the chaotic magics and beings of the void, bending them to our will.\nI will show you how to bind a servant to your will, but first you must bring me three skulls of the rattlecage skeletons near the abandoned smithy.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Imp\nExperience: 190\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Your power is little now, though I suspect already you sense the possibilities.\nEven the dead might feel alive, with that power coursing through us.","done":"Though you are still untested and young in your learning, you have proven that you possess sufficient ability to master the summoning and binding of an imp. Do not be deceived by an imp's size. Though it lacks physical strength, it possesses powers and a cleverness that will serve you well.\nAttend me carefully, ‹name›, for I will not repeat this lesson, and I will leave its mastery to you.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31,"y":66.4,"n":"Venya Marthand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7630":{"id":7630,"t":"Arcanite","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arcanite Bar to Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.\n3 Arcanite Bar","desc":"Now that the Bell, Wheel and Candle are made, I should make a black lodestone. During your ritual, you'll need that lodestone to maintain the other ritual objects if they should fail.\nTo make the lodestone, I require arcanite. Do you have any? If not, then... you'll have to get the arcanite from an alchemist.\nReturn to me when you have the arcanite, and then I'll make the black lodestone.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Do you have the arcanite, ‹name›? Once I have it I can make you the black lodestone.","done":"You got it! Nicely done! Now I can create the lodestone. When you're finally ready for your ritual to create the Circle of Greater Summoning, you'll want a lodestone to make sure the ritual doesn't fizzle out!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1710":{"id":1710,"t":"Sunscorched Shells","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Sunscorched Shells to Mathiel in Darnassus.\n20 Sunscorched Shell Sunscorched Shell","desc":"My colleague, Furen Longbeard, made a discovery which I am eager to test. I wish to try it on a new armor that I am researching, for I believe Furen's techniques will produce superior results.\nWill you help me? If you gather what I need to make the armor, then I will make an extra piece for you.\nI need the sunscorched egg shells of the Highperch Wyverns who dwell at Highperch, in Thousand Needles. Search for the shells below their nests, and return to me when you have a sufficient amount.","rew":"Experience: 1,850","back":"Do you have the shells, ‹name›? They are quite strong, and can be rendered into a lacquer I will use to coat the links of my new mail armor.","done":"Ah, thank you. These will work splendidly!\nI will begin fashioning the armor immediately...","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":59.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Mathiel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8430":{"id":8430,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5230":{"id":5230,"t":"Return to the Bulwark","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Filled Felstone Field Bottle to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Felstone Field Bottle\nProvided: Filled Felstone Field Bottle","desc":"You fill the bottle with enough of the cauldron's poisonous concoction for a suitable sample to be studied.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to Shadow Priestess Vandis at the Bulwark to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 80 0 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,650\n+50 reputation with Undercity\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Welcome back to the relative safety of the Bulwark, ‹name›. What progress on the cauldrons do you have to report?","done":"Well done ‹name› - it should take Apothecary Dithers no time at all to analyze this and devise a counter agent to introduce into the cauldron. If we are able to pump out enough of it into the air, we might be able to weaken all the Scourge present here.\nThis will no doubt be an ongoing ordeal; we will need to continually hit these cauldrons and introduce our reagents into their mix. Still, if we can keep it up, we will have a huge advantage over Scourge when the time comes for battle!\nWestern Plaguelands Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":37.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92110":{"id":92110,"t":"My first real potion","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 3 Murloc Eyes for the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.\n3 Murloc Eye","desc":"Wow, my very first potion! Did you know that mixing those two herbs together would change the potion to a bright red color when you first started?\nThat was fun, but mixing a few flowers doesn't seem like the kind of alchemy Daddy does. He uses other ingredients too.\nI don't know what else to use, so let's try the first thing that comes to mind! Let's see... maybe murloc eyes? That sounds so gross, but I bet something will happen.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Minor Discolored Healing Potion Minor Discolored Healing Potion\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 420","back":"Don't worry about me, I'm a big girl. I can take care of myself. Just don't tell anyone I am hiding here, it's our little secret.","done":"You brought me murloc eyes! I am so excited for my first REAL potion I can't breathe!\nI snuck out and grabbed a few more herbs while you were away and found some empty vials downstairs. Um... you can do the mixing this time.\n<The child watches enthusiastically you mix the ingredients, but her nose crumples as you add the eyes. The concoction takes on a sickly orange in mere seconds.>\nWow! See, I was right. I wouldn't drink that, but here's my recipe if you wanted to make more. Come back sometime!\nStart Odd Child End Odd Child Level 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 92110\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 10, 840 XP in all.\n1 [ 10 ] My First Alchemy Set\nGather 5 Empty Vials, 5 Silverleaf, and 5 Peacebloom to the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.\nOdd Child\n420 XP\n2 [ 10 ] My First Real Potion this quest\nGather 3 Murloc Eyes for the young, aspiring alchemist inside the barn of Moonbrook in Westfall.\nOdd Child\n420 XP","cats":["westfall"]},"92910":{"id":92910,"t":"Harvesting the harvesters","lv":15,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Precessive Autocognition Assembly to Ozwin Ironsprocket at Saldean's Farm.\nProvided: Precessive Autocognition Assembly","desc":"The part you managed to salvage from the harvester appears mostly intact. Someone interested in harvest golems may want to see it.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 800\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"What's this?","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":51.6,"y":32.2,"n":"Ozwin Ironsprocket","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92750":{"id":92750,"t":"Detonation at a distance","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Talk to someone in Stormwind Intelligence about acquiring a remote detonator.","desc":"I assume you want a \"controlled\" explosion? Not as much fun, but a good choice if you want to keep all your limbs.\nI'm afraid I don't have a remote detonator - why don't you go check with the sneaky folks down at Stormwind Intelligence? They should be able to find us something.","rew":"Money: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 575\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Hmm... Looking for something specific, are you?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.6,"y":8,"n":"Sprite Jumpsprocket","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.2,"y":58.8,"n":"Jasper Fel","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"6030":{"id":6030,"t":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the book, \"Studies in Spirit Speaking\", to Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff at Light's Hope Chapel, Eastern Plaguelands.\nStudies in Spirit Speaking\nProvided: Studies in Spirit Speaking","desc":"A recluse medium found in these parts by the name of Umbranse has provided the Argent Dawn with quite a literary masterpiece... one that amounts to quite possibly the largest collection of jibber-jabber I've ever seen written.\nOne of the Dawn's most respected leaders, Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff, is a brilliant linguist. Could you take this to him for me - for a reward, of course? Light's Hope Chapel - that's where he's currently at, far in the eastern part of the Eastern Plaguelands.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+50 reputation with Everlook","back":"May the Light guide you in these troubling times, ‹class›. What brings you here to this beacon of hope in the middle of darkness and despair?","done":"This... this is a very special book you have brought me. I'd like to tell you that \"special\" in this case means \"unique and quite possibly illuminating\", but that remains to be seen.\n\"Ooooooo?\" Who in their right mind thinks this up?\nWell now, I've heard of this Umbranse that Gregor spoke of, so this isn't without merit. I'll do my best to decipher it. As for you... please, have this - courtesy of the Argent Dawn. While you are here, perhaps there are some other things you can aid us with.\nWinterspring Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.3,"y":39,"n":"Gregor Greystone","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":50.1,"n":"Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"8110":{"id":8110,"t":"Enchanted South Seas Kelp","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnchanted South Seas Kelp\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"NULL","done":"See this here seaweed, mon? It be from the South Seas. We just add a little mojo and a little magic and it takes on the properties most suited to its owner.\nYou a ‹class› so it be easy, mon. Just wrap it around your neck and think of nature or squirrels or whatever it be that you people like.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]},"8190":{"id":8190,"t":"Hoodoo Hex","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring me thise things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!\nPrimal Hakkari Idol\nPunctured Voodoo Doll\nPrimal Hakkari Idol Jin'do the Hexxer in Zul'Gurub , Bloodlord Mandokir in Zul'Gurub\nPunctured Voodoo Doll Zulian Tiger 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Voodoo Slave 0.1 % in Zul'Gurub , Zulian Cub 0 % in Zul'Gurub , Atal'ai Mistress 0 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. The first is a primal Hakkari idol that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari lieutenants: Jin'do and the Bloodlord.\nThe second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed hoodoo.\nBring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","rew":"You will receive:\nHoodoo Hex\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Bring me these things and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!","done":"Use it well, ‹class›. Show the Hakkari no mercy!\nStart Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub End Zanza the Restless Zul'Gurub Level 60 , requires level 58 Difficulty 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8190","cats":["zulgurub"]}});